notes={
372588:('parked','Random G(n,c/n), fixed c>0; d-independence is generic rigidity-matroid independence, not graph degeneracy. Conjecture 7 follows the source rigidity bounds. No concentration proof for equality between MLT and the independence bound; small graph examples do not decide a high-probability assertion.'),
372609:('sustained_parked','Conjecture 5.1. S(v) is the set of sources of the induced digraph after deleting N+[v]. Universal finite nonempty sourceless oriented graphs with outdegree at most 3. See ROUTES.md: exact set test, seeded degree-preserving search, cyclic blow-up argument, and failure of the smallest-global-counterexample reduction to prove a local universal claim.'),
372683:('parked','Conjecture 5.3, every dimension d and 1<=i<=d, positive sorted real weights; covering minimum is with respect to the integer lattice. Coordinate projection gives the easy direction; arbitrary rational subspaces give the missing opposite direction. i=1 and i=d are source results, not eligible parameter instances.'),
372711:('parked','Conjecture 1.2. Integer nowhere-zero flow has conservation and magnitudes <Delta+3, all incident magnitudes distinct. General graph convention allows parallel edges. Already contains the cubic rich 6-flow problem. Assigning distinct incident labels ignores conservation; no construction survived.'),
372712:('parked','Conjecture 3.1. For a consistently oriented adjacent pair, confluent means equal signed values; contrafluent means opposite. A common universal constant is required in O(log Delta). Ordinary bounded nowhere-zero flows do not guarantee the signed separation condition. No logarithmic construction or growing lower bound found.'),
372740:('parked','Conjecture 1.3. Supremum over all singular minimizing one-phase cones, not just the O(n-k)xO(k) invariant family. Source monotonicity in k proves only the latter. Missing comparison with arbitrary cones and low-dimensional admissibility hypotheses; no source-domain counterexample used.'),
372769:('excluded_known_source_resolution','Source Propositions 2 and 3, proof bodies read: algebraic identity makes the second radicand alpha²(Delta-1)²+4Delta(1-alpha)². Squaring reduces delta>=1 case to sqrt(x)>=alpha(Delta-delta). Isolated vertices reverse the comparison. Both proof and literal domain obstruction are already in the source; no discovery credit.'),
372792:('parked','Conjecture 4.2. BSR(3,3) maximizes minimal bilinear SOS length over SOS biquadratic forms, not over all nonnegative forms. Gram matrices have freedom in the kernel of the biquadratic coefficient map. Source bounds 6 to 8 do not give rank<=6. Missing global rank reduction or explicit certified minimal rank>=7.'),
372797:('excluded_wording_route_only','Source Conjecture 5.1 retains the partition question; source (3,6)-sparsity uses the appropriate small-subset convention, unlike raw two-vertex bound which would prohibit any edge. K4 against the raw definition is only a wording correction. No counterexample to intended partition characterization; contraction parallel-edge semantics and matroid union remain gaps.'),
372894:('parked','Conjecture 1.2. Fixed k>=3, k/2<ell<k, k-ell not dividing k, all sufficiently large admissible n. Source proves ell<3k/4 range, not full scope. Missing exact absorbing argument for remaining overlap range. Finite small n obstruction is irrelevant to sufficiently large quantifier.'),
373026:('parked','Conjecture 11. Independent exponential edge costs in complete bipartite model, 1<=k<=min(m,n). Minimum matching cost has rational MGF; disk radius mn/k. Proposition 13 derives zero-freeness from nonnegative cumulants, but that is itself Conjecture 10. No unconditional cumulant proof; real positivity does not exclude complex zeros.'),
373084:('parked','Conjecture 1. Directed in-star with ell leaves and k-edge subdivided branches; universal k>=2,ell>=1. Theorem 2 proves directed k=2 only. Greedy paths can consume branch roots and do not prove the sharp oriented half-threshold. No full-scope mechanism.'),
373130:('parked','Conjecture 7.14, every fixed H of treewidth 2. H-process adds all missing edges completing a copy of H in synchronous rounds; M_H maximizes over n-vertex initial graphs. Tree decompositions do not bound time without control of repeated separators. Missing linear bound for arbitrary partial 2-trees.'),
373131:('parked','Conjecture 8.5, conjunction of exponent 3/2 for K3,3 and Q3. Source Proposition 8.1 reduces to extremal-number upper bounds which do not close either case. No improving infection-chain estimate; one small running-time instance cannot refute asymptotics.'),
373145:('parked','Classical El-Zahar cycle-cover conjecture, all prescribed integer cycle lengths >=3 summing to n. Source is motivation in a digraph paper; no full prescribed-cycle construction. Dirac gives one cycle only and cannot be iterated at the same degree threshold.'),
373162:('parked','Conjecture 6.3, mirror-deformed Markov triples in the source tree with degree in q. Source equation and branch deformation are essential; ordinary Markov integer uniqueness is not the same claim. No injectivity invariant recovered; identifying permutations of one triple is a convention correction only.'),
373195:('parked','Conjecture 4.1, one epsilon>0 and infinitely many n, connected vertex-transitive digraphs with n-circumference>=epsilon*n. Source supplies logarithmic gap. Need a vertex-transitive amplification retaining a positive gap ratio; Cartesian/lexicographic products may create much longer cycles.'),
373206:('parked','Conjecture 6.2, dissociated means no nontrivial {-1,0,1} relation; dimension maximum size. Both log² global dimension and positive-density log-dimensional subset required, uniformly for fixed K and sufficiently large N. Source log³ estimate does not supply either sharp endpoint.'),
373215:('excluded_known_source_resolution','Current source Part V Theorem 16.3 proves empirical zero measures converge to a law with positive mass in every (0,epsilon). Hence eventually some zero lies below epsilon, so smallest zero tends to zero. This direct bridge uses only the proved limiting distribution, not the informal fixed-index n^-2 asymptotics. No new theorem.'),
373225:('parked','Conjecture 4.2 for four listed exceptional singularity families. R(f) denotes exponents removed from spectrum to obtain Tjurina spectrum, not arbitrary two largest Milnor algebra monomials. Missing uniform Newton-degenerate spectrum calculation with allowed normal-form parameter ranges; no Lean feasible reduction recovered.'),
373229:('excluded_known_source_refutation','Source section 4.2 explicitly recalls the earlier refutation by Stevanovic-Damnjanovic-Stevanovic arXiv:2111.15303 and exhibits order-14 counterexamples itself. Universal energy bound is already false, not a fresh target. Earlier paper body not audited independently; cited source supplies same-scope counterexamples.'),
373230:('sustained_parked','Source Conjecture 4.3. Mo=sum over edges |number closer to u minus number closer to v|. See ROUTES.md for exact distance blow-up reduction, tests, diameter-two structural identity, and comparison with primary 2210.03399 and 2211.06682. No full graph compression theorem or witness.'),
373286:('parked','Prior unindexed history found in sol-fresh-source-discovery-r124/sources/original-00.md: 42,767 exact constructed triples already searched without counterexample. No repeated search performed. Unnumbered conjecture on the specific q-rational construction of polynomial Pythagorean triples, not every polynomial solution of A²+B²=C². Unimodality known for q-rationals does not automatically survive the products and combinations used here. Need complete coefficient formula and closure inequality; no eligible proof.'),
373308:('sustained_parked','Conjecture 1, all prime powers q, n=q²+q+1. Current source classification says polarity graphs with exactly q+1 absolute points, broader wording than MathDB orthogonal polarity. See ROUTES.md: exact atlas n=7, greedy n=13,21, spectral pair argument and residual global determinant inequality. No scope-widened classification counterexample claimed.'),
373339:('parked_conditional_source_theorem','Current TeX Theorem labelled conj:fac proves equality of divisor map and smallest face map, but its proof explicitly assumes the divisor conjecture divconj. Read proof: invertibility of semigroup character at a stratum is equivalent to its divisor missing that stratum, then to orthogonality to all containing extremal rays. This is conditional evidence, not an unconditional full resolution. Missing applicable divisor conjecture in all source hypotheses.'),
373350:('parked','Conjecture 5.1, fixed c>1/2, asymptotic n, proper edge coloring, n/8 Hamilton cycles each with cn-o(n) colors. Full packing constraints and uniform error term matter; repeating one Hamilton cycle is not an eligible wording solution. Source one colorful cycle theorem cannot simply be iterated as degree falls.'),
373406:('parked','Conjecture 5.7. Extremal ML threshold from Huesler-Reiss covariance completion vs Gaussian MLT on each undirected graph. Chordal and C4 computations motivate relation but do not establish universal equality. Missing exact rank/completion semantic relation; no endpoint from a surrogate matrix invariant.'),
373420:('parked','Asymptotic Aharoni-Berger-Kfir acyclic-set bound; an acyclic set is a vertex subset inducing no directed cycle. Tournament specialization would improve the classical factor 2 gap. Random ordering yields the weaker scale only; no sharp entropy argument.'),
373458:('parked','Source conjecture on Cox(mu)^K with adjoined maximum. Current main theorem proves shellability of the augmented whole admissible set, not automatically its Coxeter subset: EL-shellability is not hereditary to arbitrary subposets. Missing restricted labeling proof; no corollary asserted.'),
373471:('excluded_changed_source_range','Raw n>rs differs from current source Conjecture 2, n>2rs. Acknowledgments explicitly state obstruction for n<=rs+1. An old-range counterexample would repeat known source correction. Current intended sharp range not solved; no proof credit claimed.'),
373478:('parked','Source section 3.2 algorithm enumerates neighborhoods of a minimum-degree vertex (at most 5) and checks exact deck equality. Polynomially many candidates does not prove unique reconstruction; exact deck comparison and isomorphism also need complexity bridges. No injectivity proof for this planar class; experimental success not proof.'),
373523:('excluded_known_source_resolution','Current source Theorem 1 is exactly Bialy conjecture. Proposition 2 gives a unique analytic eccentricity family fixing beta(rho0), Proposition 3 proves strict monotonicity of beta(rho1) along it by nonvanishing integral comparison. Theorem 1 and Proposition 3 proof body inspected. No discovery credit.'),
373532:('excluded_known_source_resolution','Conjecture 5.2 is explicitly proved via Proposition 5.3 for R-disjoint graphs, which include almost bipartite non-KE graphs. Proof read: restrict maximum matching to G[R(C)] using Lemma 3.11; Lemma 3.14 gives non-KE almost bipartite component, flower/blossom theorem forces floor(|C|/2) matched cycle edges. This is already source resolution.'),
373539:('excluded_wording_route_only','Source discussion after Theorem 3.14 and Theorem 3.16 makes intended hypothesis simultaneous minimal k- and (k+1)-{1,2}-factor-criticality. Reading t as either one alone gives easy noncomplete examples but is a wording correction. Intended planar case k=1 is already proved in source; no general proof.'),
373550:('parked','Conjecture 3.1 for nontrivial qubit PI codes correcting weight t; KL conditions for 2t deletions are source semantics. Numerical minimal lengths 7,19,37,61,91 are not lower bounds. Need either exact KL infeasibility below quadratic length or a shorter explicit code. t=0/domain and distance parity changes are excluded corrections.'),
373551:('excluded_basis_convention_route','Conjecture 3.2 on real coefficients in Dicke basis. Source explicitly allows global minus signs, so negating a codeword does not make a meaningful new counterexample. Logical basis changes and representative phase conventions must be quotiented before judging the symmetry. No substantive code-subspace obstruction or minimality proof recovered.'),
373591:('excluded_known_source_refutation','Source section 6.1 gives Haim-Kislev-Ostrover regular pentagon example: c=1 and area K*area Q=(5/(sqrt5+3))*c²/2<c²/2. Full explicit source argument read using Q-normal triangles and Theorem 3.3. This is known refutation, not an open discovery.'),
373592:('parked','Conjecture 2.2, planar convex bodies K with Euclidean shortest generalized closed billiard length 1. Source connects Mallée parabolic triangle to Wetzel worm problem. Polygon discretization does not bound all convex tables or beat example rigorously. No admissible smaller-area billiard-certified shape.'),
373596:('parked','Source Conjecture 1.8. Universal 4-connected induced-{K1,4,K1,4+e}-free graphs with delta>=6. Source result covers split graphs of order>=13 only. Equivalent source line-graph conjecture is equally hard; small arbitrary nonhamiltonian graphs fail connectivity or forbidden induced-subgraph hypotheses.'),
373597:('parked','Source Conjecture 1.9. Universal 4-connected line graphs with delta>=5. Weaker than Thomassen but still tied to dominating Eulerian subgraphs. Source states equivalence to Conjecture 1.8, not resolution. No suitable 4-edge-connected root graph with provably absent dominating Eulerian subgraph.')}
